# Contact form. Copy to .env.local for development; set the same three in the
# Vercel project for production. See app/api/contact/route.ts and README.
#
# ALL THREE ARE OPTIONAL AT BUILD TIME and the build does not read them. With
# RESEND_API_KEY missing the route answers 503 and the form tells the visitor
# to email the address directly, naming it. It never reports success without
# sending.
#
# ONLY RESEND_API_KEY IS ACTUALLY REQUIRED AT RUNTIME. CONTACT_FROM used to be
# as well, with no default, which is what broke the form in production: it was
# never set, so every submission answered 503 and told the sender the form was
# not connected. The route now falls back to noreply@ on the verified domain.

# resend.com → API Keys. Sending permission is enough; it does not need full
# access. Starts "re_".
RESEND_API_KEY=

# The From address. OPTIONAL: app/api/contact/route.ts defaults to
# "Portfolio <noreply@trevorriggle.design>", which is on the verified domain.
# Set this only to send from a different address or a different domain.
#
# It MUST be on a domain verified in Resend, and it must not be the gmail
# address: the sender's own address rides in Reply-To, and a From header
# claiming to be gmail.com from a domain that is not gmail.com is how a
# sending reputation gets burned.
#
# To send before verifying a domain, Resend's shared test sender works:
#   CONTACT_FROM=onboarding@resend.dev
# with the caveat that it will only deliver to the address the Resend account
# itself is registered to. Fine for proving the wiring, not for production.
CONTACT_FROM=

# Where the mail lands. Optional: defaults to site.email in lib/site.ts.
CONTACT_TO=
